egative infinity. Original option 0 is correct and agrees with stored 'Diverges'. The reported difference is wording, not a mathematical contradiction. This is a source-backed derived judgment."} {"question" "q-115511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-2)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(y-4)"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "4fb8e5c4946e737c7fded9b0e532d60c1cb37f6fb365cfeb6698aae22306fb1b" "reviewer_session" "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca" "rationale" "Substitution of (4,1) into (x-2)^2=4p(y-4) gives 4=-12p, so p=-1/3. Original option 2 follows. Solving for y gives the stored y=-3/4(x-2)^2+4 exactly; the unresolved comparison does not imply a wrong key. This source-backed derived review supplies authoritative provenance for the captured representation." "bindings" {"problem" "77c6cb180abbe9877c3b2083a582ac0435831be15c240f95c36ed5d310189e90" "worked_solution" "b843fcb3ead6c57abe6e5546629622f7323e6b9a5758823bd3e873413a9f0efb" "original_field" "c2a4cba10680607d1af446e0962e8e39e2ca197adee2d0b6648363a8b7e46f87" "reviewed_field" "f6bbb2c18f4abc98e2aae9d5e99ac16ef753d1be904854867ec2c6f8e35271dc" "raw_widget" "a9f53f00b6d869f20c2097fa089b743ea979ade4e8098c813a91f8ba9a880007"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "question-034-before.png" "sha256" "6d321102e76ed54b47648ef8bc81b0978075eec5ab08e560c4a7ea8a71075a74"} {"path" "question-034-after.json" "sha256" "b646a68d5924c2e5c8cbcbec9cb356bb2b887c682860fca000e14cc30f5ae8c7"} {"path" "history-q-115511.png" "sha256" "c70d50a82a59213111e8a7e64823752b58e09f46ef8c79edeb409ef68a29b7f7"}]} {"question" "q-115511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+2)^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}(y+4)"] ["math" "(x+2)^{2}=3(y+4)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}(y-4)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(y-4)"] ["math" "(x-4)^{2}=4(y-2)"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file